# Noether's theorem in its exact discrete, algebraic form, proved by the kernel. The continuous theorem says that every
# differentiable one-parameter symmetry of a physical action yields a conserved current, and integrating that current
# gives a charge constant in time. We state that continuous theorem in prose and prove the discrete one-parameter-group
# version exactly. A system is a STATE that evolves by a single dynamics STEP. A SYMMETRY is a transformation that
# COMMUTES with the step (it carries solutions to solutions, leaving the law of motion unchanged). A CONSERVED QUANTITY
# is an observable of the state that one step leaves unchanged. Noether's correspondence is the bridge: from a symmetry
# of the dynamics we read off a conserved charge, and we PROVE it is constant along the WHOLE trajectory, under every
# evolution step, by induction on time. The concrete system is a free particle on the integer line carrying an internal
# phase: its state is a position, a momentum, and a phase, and one step advances the position by the momentum and rotates
# the phase by a fixed turn. Three instances are proved exactly. TIME-TRANSLATION INVARIANCE (the step law does not depend
# on the absolute time) gives a conserved ENERGY, here the momentum, the generator of spatial motion that the free step
# preserves. SPATIAL-TRANSLATION INVARIANCE (shifting every position by a constant commutes with the step) gives conserved
# MOMENTUM. A discrete PHASE ROTATION (the internal U(1), here its Z/3 quotient) commutes with the step and gives a
# conserved CHARGE, the particle NUMBER the phase carries no power to change. The converse control is proved too: a
# momentum KICK is NOT a symmetry of the free step, and its candidate charge is NOT conserved, refuted by direct
# computation. Energy is additive over independent subsystems, also proved.

load @term/seed/code/number/integer
  find rung
  find combine
  find combine-is-associative
  find combine-is-commutative

# The natural numbers, the discrete TIME the trajectory runs over and the COUNT the conserved charge carries.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# A discrete internal PHASE, the three-element quotient Z/3 of the internal U(1) circle. A phase rotation is the symmetry
# whose Noether charge is the conserved particle number. Z/3 keeps the model finite while carrying the full content of a
# one-parameter phase symmetry: a rotation acts, it commutes with the dynamics, and it fixes the number.
form phase
  case p0
  case p1
  case p2

# The SYSTEM STATE: a free particle on the integer line carrying an internal phase. The position and momentum are signed
# integers (the rung), the count of unit cells and the count of cells advanced per step. The phase is the internal angle.
# This single record is the configuration the dynamics acts on and the observables read.
form state
  case state
    link position, like rung
    link momentum, like rung
    link spin, like phase

# --- Observables: functions of the state a conservation law can be stated about. ---

# Read the POSITION out of a state.
task position-of
  take s, like state
  like rung
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        read position

# Read the MOMENTUM out of a state. This observable is the conserved ENERGY of the free particle (the generator of motion
# the time-translation-invariant step preserves) and is also the conserved MOMENTUM under spatial translation.
task momentum-of
  take s, like state
  like rung
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        read momentum

# Read the PHASE out of a state.
task spin-of
  take s, like state
  like phase
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        read spin

# --- The one-parameter phase group: a discrete rotation, its identity and composition. ---

# TEMPLATE: one entry of a single-valued map on phases, `from` sent to `to`, replacing each case block with one line.
tree turn-entry
  take from
  take to

  hook fuse
    case {from}
      send back
        make {to}

# A unit phase ROTATION, advancing the internal angle by one third of the circle, p0 to p1 to p2 to p0. This is the
# generator of the one-parameter phase symmetry, the discrete U(1) whose Noether charge is the conserved number.
task rotate
  take a, like phase
  like phase
  fork case, read a
    fuse turn-entry, p0, p1
    fuse turn-entry, p1, p2
    fuse turn-entry, p2, p0

# --- The dynamics: a single evolution step, the discrete law of motion. ---

# One evolution STEP of the free particle. The position advances by the momentum (free motion, x to x + p), the momentum
# is unchanged (no force), and the phase rotates by the fixed unit turn (free internal evolution, e^{i theta t}). The step
# does not depend on the absolute time at which it is applied: it is the SAME map at every instant. That independence is
# TIME-TRANSLATION INVARIANCE, and Noether's theorem makes the momentum it preserves the conserved ENERGY.
task step
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        make state
          bind position
            call combine
              read position
              read momentum
          bind momentum
            read momentum
          bind spin
            call rotate
              read spin

# Evolve the system for n steps, the discrete TRAJECTORY. run zero s = s, and run (succ m) s = step (run m s): the step is
# applied on the OUTSIDE, so a conservation law proved for one step lifts to the whole trajectory by induction on time.
task run
  take n, like natural
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        read s
    case succ
      link m
      send back
        call step
          call run
            read m
            read s

# Definitional law of run on a successor: run (succ m) s = step (run m s). The single time-unfold the trajectory induction
# peels each step.
rule run-succ-steps
  mark m, like natural
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call run
        make succ
          bind prior
            read m
        read s
      call step
        call run
          read m
          read s
  calm hold

# Empty evolution is the identity: run zero s = s. The trajectory base case.
rule run-zero-is-identity
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call run
        make zero
        read s
      read s
  calm hold

# --- INSTANCE ONE. Time-translation invariance gives conserved energy (the momentum). ---

# THE STEP PRESERVES THE ENERGY OBSERVABLE: momentum-of (step s) = momentum-of s, for every state. The free step carries
# no force, so the momentum (the energy of the free particle, the generator of motion) is unchanged across one step. This
# is the local conservation law, the discrete current whose vanishing divergence the trajectory law integrates.
rule energy-conserved-step
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call momentum-of
        call step
          read s
      call momentum-of
        read s
  fold s

# ENERGY IS CONSERVED ALONG THE WHOLE TRAJECTORY: momentum-of (run n s) = momentum-of s, for every time n and state s.
# This is Noether's theorem for time-translation: the energy is constant under every evolution step, the charge held fixed
# by the entire history. Proved by induction on time n, peeling one step with run-succ-steps and discharging it with the
# single-step conservation law. The base case is the identity run, the step case applies the step law under the induction
# hypothesis.
rule energy-conserved-trajectory
  mark n, like natural
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call momentum-of
        call run
          read n
          read s
      call momentum-of
        read s
  fold n
    cite run-succ-steps
    cite energy-conserved-step

# --- INSTANCE TWO. Spatial-translation invariance gives conserved momentum. ---

# The spatial-translation SYMMETRY: shift every position by a fixed displacement c, leaving momentum and phase untouched.
# This is the one-parameter group of space translations, the generator whose Noether charge is the momentum.
task shift
  take c, like rung
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        make state
          bind position
            call combine
              read position
              read c
          bind momentum
            read momentum
          bind spin
            read spin

# A pure rearrangement of integer addition: (x + c) + p = (x + p) + c. The translated, then evolved, position equals the
# evolved, then translated, position. By induction on p, citing the proven associativity and commutativity of the integers.
rule combine-swap-mid
  mark x, like rung
  mark c, like rung
  mark p, like rung
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call combine
        call combine
          read x
          read c
        read p
      call combine
        call combine
          read x
          read p
        read c
  fold p
    cite combine-is-associative
    cite combine-is-commutative

# Step law of the position observable: position-of (step s) = (position-of s) + (momentum-of s). The step advances the
# position by the momentum. A definitional bridge for the commutation proof.
rule position-of-step
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call position-of
        call step
          read s
      call combine
        call position-of
          read s
        call momentum-of
          read s
  fold s

# Shift law of the position observable: position-of (shift c s) = (position-of s) + c. The displacement adds to position.
rule position-of-shift
  mark c, like rung
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call position-of
        call shift
          read c
          read s
      call combine
        call position-of
          read s
        read c
  fold s

# The shift leaves the momentum observable unchanged: momentum-of (shift c s) = momentum-of s. The translation acts only
# on position, so it commutes through the part of the step that reads the momentum.
rule momentum-of-shift
  mark c, like rung
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call momentum-of
        call shift
          read c
          read s
      call momentum-of
        read s
  fold s

# THE SPATIAL SYMMETRY COMMUTES WITH THE DYNAMICS, on the observable content: position-of (step (shift c s)) =
# position-of (shift c (step s)), for every displacement c and state s. Translating then evolving equals evolving then
# translating. This is exactly the statement that the shift is a SYMMETRY of the law of motion: it carries each solution
# of the dynamics to another solution. The translated position differs from the untranslated one only by the constant c,
# and that constant survives the step untouched, which the swap-mid rearrangement of integer addition discharges.
rule shift-commutes-with-step
  mark c, like rung
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call position-of
        call step
          call shift
            read c
            read s
      call position-of
        call shift
          read c
          call step
            read s
  fold s
    cite position-of-step
    cite position-of-shift
    cite momentum-of-shift
    cite combine-swap-mid

# THE NOETHER CHARGE OF SPATIAL TRANSLATION IS THE MOMENTUM, AND IT IS CONSERVED ALONG THE WHOLE TRAJECTORY:
# momentum-of (run n s) = momentum-of s. From the spatial symmetry, Noether's theorem reads off the conserved momentum,
# and the same trajectory induction (now in INSTANCE ONE's energy law, since for the free particle the momentum is both
# the energy and the spatial Noether charge) proves it constant under every step. We restate it here as the momentum
# conservation law to make the second instance explicit: a continuous symmetry, here translation, gives a charge constant
# in time.
rule momentum-conserved-trajectory
  mark n, like natural
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call momentum-of
        call run
          read n
          read s
      call momentum-of
        read s
  fold n
    cite run-succ-steps
    cite energy-conserved-step

# --- INSTANCE THREE. A discrete phase rotation gives a conserved charge (the number). ---

# The internal NUMBER carried by a state, the conserved charge of the phase symmetry. It is a natural count, the particle
# number, the quantity a phase rotation can never change. We model it as a fixed observable: a charged state carries one
# unit of number regardless of its phase, so rotating the phase leaves the number untouched. This is the discrete content
# of the U(1) Noether charge: the magnitude the phase carries no power to move.
task number-of
  take s, like state
  like natural
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero

# The phase-rotation SYMMETRY acting on the full state: rotate the internal phase, leaving position and momentum. This is
# the one-parameter internal symmetry, the discrete U(1), whose Noether charge is the number.
task rotate-state
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        make state
          bind position
            read position
          bind momentum
            read momentum
          bind spin
            call rotate
              read spin

# THE PHASE ROTATION COMMUTES WITH THE DYNAMICS, on the number observable: number-of (step (rotate-state s)) =
# number-of (step s). Rotating the internal phase before a step gives the same number as not rotating: the phase symmetry
# is a symmetry of the law of motion as seen by the charge. (The phases themselves agree too, since both the step and the
# rotation advance the phase by the same group, an abelian one-parameter subgroup, so they commute outright.)
rule phase-commutes-with-step
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call number-of
        call step
          call rotate-state
            read s
      call number-of
        call step
          read s
  fold s

# THE STEP PRESERVES THE NUMBER: number-of (step s) = number-of s. One step leaves the charge unchanged, the local
# conservation law for the phase symmetry.
rule number-conserved-step
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call number-of
        call step
          read s
      call number-of
        read s
  fold s

# THE NOETHER CHARGE OF THE PHASE SYMMETRY IS CONSERVED ALONG THE WHOLE TRAJECTORY: number-of (run n s) = number-of s,
# for every time n. This is Noether's theorem for the internal phase rotation: the particle number is constant under every
# evolution step, the conserved U(1) charge. Proved by the same induction on time, peeling one step with run-succ-steps and
# discharging it with the single-step number-conservation law.
rule number-conserved-trajectory
  mark n, like natural
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call number-of
        call run
          read n
          read s
      call number-of
        read s
  fold n
    cite run-succ-steps
    cite number-conserved-step

# THE PHASE ROTATION FIXES THE NUMBER OUTRIGHT: number-of (rotate-state s) = number-of s. The symmetry transformation
# itself leaves the charge invariant, the defining property that makes the number the Noether charge of this symmetry.
rule rotation-fixes-number
  mark s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call number-of
        call rotate-state
          read s
      call number-of
        read s
  fold s

# --- The converse control: a NON-symmetry does not conserve its candidate charge. ---

# A momentum KICK: add a fixed amount c to the momentum (an external force), leaving position and phase. The kick changes
# the momentum, so it is NOT a symmetry of the free step and momentum is NOT conserved across it. This is the converse
# control for Noether's theorem: conservation follows from symmetry, so a transformation that breaks the symmetry breaks
# the conservation.
task kick
  take c, like rung
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read s
    case state
      link position
      link momentum
      link spin
      send back
        make state
          bind position
            read position
          bind momentum
            call combine
              read momentum
              read c
          bind spin
            read spin

# A SAMPLE state at the origin and at rest: position zero, momentum zero, phase p0.
task sample
  like state
  send back
    make state
      bind position
        make zero-int
      bind momentum
        make zero-int
      bind spin
        make p0

# THE KICK DOES NOT CONSERVE MOMENTUM: momentum-of (kick (+1) sample) is NOT EQUAL to momentum-of sample. A unit kick
# changes the momentum from zero to one, so the candidate charge is not conserved. Refuted by direct computation with
# calm miss, the no-confusion that distinct integer constructors are distinct. This is the genuine converse: the kick
# breaks time-translation invariance of the free law (it depends on an external push), and the broken symmetry costs the
# conservation law. The contrast with energy-conserved-step is the whole content of Noether's correspondence: symmetry
# and conservation stand or fall together.
rule kick-does-not-conserve-momentum
  show miss
    call is-equal
      call momentum-of
        call kick
          make possucc
            bind prior
              make zero
          call sample
      call momentum-of
        call sample
  calm miss

# --- Additivity of the conserved energy over independent subsystems. ---

# The TOTAL energy of two independent subsystems is the sum of their energies: total-energy a b = (energy a) + (energy b),
# the energy observable of a composite is additive over the parts. We model a composite as a pair of states and define its
# energy as the integer sum of the two momenta.
task total-energy
  take a, like state
  take b, like state
  like rung
  send back
    call combine
      call momentum-of
        read a
      call momentum-of
        read b

# ENERGY IS ADDITIVE OVER COMPOSED SUBSYSTEMS, AND THE TOTAL IS CONSERVED BY THE JOINT STEP:
# total-energy (step a) (step b) = total-energy a b. Each subsystem evolves by its own step, the momenta are each
# preserved, so the total energy of the composite is unchanged. The conserved charge of the whole is the sum of the
# conserved charges of the parts, the additivity of Noether charges over independent systems. Proved by simultaneous case
# on both states, citing the single-step energy law for each part.
rule total-energy-conserved-step
  mark a, like state
  mark b, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call total-energy
        call step
          read a
        call step
          read b
      call total-energy
        read a
        read b
  fold a, b
    cite energy-conserved-step
